# Ownership is the last line of defence when a change is textually innocuous but
# semantically a policy change. The canonical example lives in versions.json:
# widening a track from ^3\.90\.[0-9]+-ubi$ to ^3\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+-ubi$ is a
# one-character-class edit, indistinguishable at a glance from a routine digest
# bump, that silently converts every future minor release from a reviewed
# decision into an automated bump.
#
# NOTE: two teams on one line means EITHER may approve, not both. GitHub has no
# "one approval from each team" primitive. Genuine dual control here comes from
# Required Reviewers on the Review-Actor and Release-Actor environments, not
# from this file.
#
# All three teams must exist and have repository access, or CODEOWNERS matches
# nothing and "require review from Code Owners" becomes a silent no-op. Verify
# with: gh api orgs/infrashift/teams/<slug> --jq .slug

*                                   @infrashift/platform-engineers

# --- Trust decisions -------------------------------------------------------
# versions.json carries trust classes, track constraints, digest pins and
# source commits. Every one of those is a security decision.
/versions.json                      @infrashift/security-admins
/schemas/                           @infrashift/security-admins

/.github/pdp/                       @infrashift/security-admins
/.github/pdp/policies.rego          @infrashift/security-admins
/.github/pdp/policies_test.rego     @infrashift/security-admins
/.github/pdp/keyring/               @infrashift/security-admins
/.github/pdp/public-keys/           @infrashift/security-admins

# Exceptions are the ONLY CVE-shaped knob in the system. Platform engineers
# raise them; security admins must also be able to review.
/.github/pdp/exceptions.yaml        @infrashift/security-admins @infrashift/platform-engineers

# --- Pipeline engines ------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/                 @infrashift/devops-leads @infrashift/security-admins
/.github/actions/                   @infrashift/devops-leads @infrashift/security-admins
/scripts/                           @infrashift/devops-leads

# A Containerfile change alters what lands inside a trusted image.
/Containerfiles/                    @infrashift/devops-leads @infrashift/security-admins
# Baked-in service config ships in the image and is therefore part of it.
/rootfs/                            @infrashift/devops-leads @infrashift/security-admins

/Ops.mk                             @infrashift/devops-leads

# --- Repository security posture -------------------------------------------
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @infrashift/security-admins
/.gitleaks.toml                     @infrashift/security-admins
/.gitignore                         @infrashift/security-admins
/SETUP-ENVIRONMENTS.md              @infrashift/security-admins

# --- Documentation ---------------------------------------------------------
/docs/                              @infrashift/platform-engineers
/.ai/                               @infrashift/platform-engineers
/CLAUDE.md                          @infrashift/platform-engineers
/README.md                          @infrashift/platform-engineers
